---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Why these figures differ from others" activeNav="differences">
  <Fragment slot="masthead">
    <h1>Why these figures differ from others</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Two sources can both be right and still give different numbers, because they count different things. This
      page says what each one counts. It does not try to make the figures match.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Registrations are not sales</h2>
    <p>
      A vehicle is counted in the month it was first registered, not the month it was ordered, paid for or handed
      over. A vehicle can be registered before it is sold.{" "}
      <a href="/method#data-grains">What the charts count</a>.{" "}
      <a href="/caveats">Registered is not the same as sold</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Survivors are not registrations</h2>
    <p>
      Most charts count vehicles first registered in a month that are still registered at the latest snapshot.
      Vehicles that have left the register since are not in the count, so a count for an older month is smaller than the
      number first registered then. The charts of true registrations count every vehicle first registered, including
      those since removed, and the two are never drawn together. <a href="/method#data-grains">The ways to count the register</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope can differ</h2>
    <p>
      This site counts only some vehicle types, and only vehicles registered in New Zealand for the first time.
      A source that counts other types, or counts returning vehicles, will give a different total. This site
      leaves out buses, motor caravans and special purpose vehicles, among others, so its total of new vehicles is
      lower than a total that counts them.{" "}
      <a href="/method#vehicle-scope">Which vehicles are counted</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The Motor Industry Association's figures</h2>
    <p>
      The Motor Industry Association (MIA) publishes a count of new vehicle registrations each month. Set beside
      this site's true registrations of new vehicles, its count is a little higher. Two things have been measured.
      Adding new buses, motor caravans and special purpose vehicles to this site's new goods vehicles comes close
      to the MIA's commercial count in the months compared. What is left is small for recent months and wider for
      older ones. The MIA's figures are as reported when a month closed, or as it later restates them; this
      site's are as NZTA's dashboard holds them at the latest export, where NZTA says a past month can gain or
      lose vehicles. Whether that accounts for all of the older gap is not established. The charts that count
      vehicles still registered are lower again, as the section above says. This site does not adjust a figure to
      match another source.
    </p>

    <h2>Other sites take a different source</h2>
    <p>
      Some other sites take first registrations from NZTA's registrations dashboard. This site reads that dashboard
      too, for the charts of true registrations where a build has them, and the open register for everything else. A site that counts only
      the dashboard, or only the register, will give a different figure for the same month.{" "}
      <a href="/method#true-registrations">What true registrations count</a>.{" "}
      <a href="/caveats">Other limits of the data</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>If a figure here still looks wrong</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/feedback">Report it</a>, with the page address and the figure you expected.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
